outputs.L2:
A cardiac surgery apparatus is described that includes:  

a) multiple pairs of suture guides arranged at intervals around a frame;  

b) multiple suture tubes, each tube being associated with a respective pair of suture guides;  

c) multiple snares, with each snare assigned to and extending through one of the suture tubes, such that a handle on one end of the snare extends out from the proximal end of its corresponding suture tube, while a snare loop on the opposite end extends out through the distal end of that suture tube, the snare loop also passing through one suture guide of the associated pair; and  

d) multiple sutures, each matched with one of the suture-guide pairs and attached to the guide in that pair through which the snare loop does not pass.

counterfactuals.output:
A cardiac surgery apparatus comprising:

a plurality of suture guide pairs, each suture guide pair including a first suture guide and a second suture guide configured to be positioned relative to cardiac tissue;

a plurality of suture tubes, each suture tube being associated with a respective one of the plurality of suture guide pairs and defining a lumen extending therethrough;

a plurality of snares, each snare extending through the lumen of a respective one of the plurality of suture tubes, each snare including a snare loop disposed adjacent one suture guide of the associated suture guide pair; and

a plurality of sutures, each suture being associated with the other suture guide of the associated suture guide pair, the other suture guide being a suture guide of the pair not occupied by the snare loop,

wherein each snare is configured to capture or engage a corresponding suture associated with the suture guide not occupied by the snare loop, and to draw the corresponding suture through the respective suture tube, thereby facilitating placement or manipulation of the sutures during a cardiac surgical procedure.
